{"etape": 15, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T14:46:24.731711Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I've reviewed all three reservations. Here's what I found:\n\n**1. NQNU5R (MCO → SEA, business, 2 passengers)** — The flights HAT214 (May 13) and HAT045 (May 14) have **already landed**, so I'm unable to cancel this reservation. This requires a human agent.\n\n**2. IFOYYZ (CLT → EWR round trip, basic economy, 1 passenger)** — This booking was created on 2024-05-12 (more than 24 hours ago), the cabin is basic economy, there is no travel insurance, and both flights (HAT157 on May 28, HAT215 on May 30) are still operating normally. Under policy, none of the cancellation conditions apply, so I'm unable to cancel it. Could you tell me the reason for cancellation in case something changes?\n\n**3. M20IZO (JFK → MCO, economy, 2 passengers)** — Both flights (HAT268 and HAT010 on 2024-05-22) are still upcoming, so a cabin upgrade to **business** is possible. Current business fares for these flights are $430 + $412 = $842 per passenger, versus the original $245 per passenger. That's an estimated **additional charge of $1,194 total** for 2 passengers.\n\nTo proceed with the upgrade, please confirm:\n- **Yes, upgrade M20IZO to business class** (keeping the same flights and date)\n- Which payment method to use for the difference: **Mastercard ending 7334** (credit_card_9074831) or **Mastercard ending 5018** (credit_card_4959530)?"}, "resultat": "Okay, I understand about NQNU5R and IFOYYZ. That's a bit disappointing, but I appreciate you checking the policies.\n\nRegarding M20IZO, yes, please go ahead and upgrade it to business class. I'd like to use my credit card ending in 7334 for the additional charge.", "erreur": null}
