{"etape": 18, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T14:46:47.057620Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "I understand the frustration. Here's the honest breakdown:\n\n**IFOYYZ (CLT → EWR, basic economy)** — There is no \"cancel with a fee\" option in our policy. A cancellation is only permitted if one of these applies:\n- Booking made within the last 24 hours (this one was created 2024-05-12, three days ago)\n- The airline cancelled the flight (both HAT157 and HAT215 are still operating)\n- It's a business cabin booking (this is basic economy)\n- The traveler has travel insurance and the reason is covered (no insurance on this booking)\n\nSince none apply, I genuinely cannot cancel it — and unfortunately basic economy fares are also non-modifiable, so I can't change the flights on it either.\n\n**NQNU5R (MCO → SEA, business)** — This one *would* normally qualify for cancellation since it's business class, but both flight segments (HAT214 on May 13 and HAT045 on May 14) have already landed. Once any portion of a trip has been flown, I have no ability to cancel or refund it in the system — only a human agent can review it.\n\nIf you'd like, I can transfer you to a human agent to look into NQNU5R. Just let me know."}, "resultat": "Okay, I appreciate you explaining that in detail. It's clear now why those can't be canceled through the system.\n\nYes, please transfer me to a human agent to discuss NQNU5R. Maybe they can offer some alternative.###TRANSFER###", "erreur": null}
